# Cloudflare Pages response headers for static files. Hand-written: the Python build never writes or touches this file.
# Pages applies _headers to static assets only. The Functions pages (/proof/*, /order/*) set their own headers in
# functions/_lib/util.js (X-Frame-Options, a CSP with frame-ancestors, no-store, noindex).
#
# Only safe headers here: no full Content-Security-Policy (it could break the 3D designer or the Stripe redirect).
# Strict-Transport-Security is short on purpose (5 minutes, no includeSubDomains, no preload). Once the site has run
# on HTTPS for a while it can be raised, for example to 15552000 (6 months), still without preload.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300

/proof/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

/order/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

/admin*
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Keep the *.pages.dev copies (production and per-deploy URLs) out of search results. This replaces the old
# functions/_middleware.js, which ran a Function on every request just to add this header.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
